1.Write a bash or fish script that takes two arguments argument1, argument2 which can come from
the command line or declared inside the script.
2.argument1 is a filename for input .e.g. usernames.txt, which contains a list of usernames.
3.argument2 is a string, i.e. the name of a file to look for in the users’ home directory.
The script reads users from usernames.txt and returns for each user and the filename argument2
4) “File not found” if the file is not there.
5) “Permission denied” if there is no access to the home folder of the user.
6) “File found, size xxxx bytes” if file is found.
The script would be invoked like this ./myscript.sh usernames.txt “tarbal.tar.gz” , or in
the case of the variables being declared inside the script the script is invoked by ./myscript.sh
